# Line endings, at the Git level.
#
# The monorepo baseline in .editorconfig is CRLF, which is right for every file
# a person edits on either side. It is wrong for two generated ones: a shell
# script with CRLF endings does not run on the Linux CI runner, and `gradlew` is
# a shell script that the Android jobs invoke directly. `.editorconfig` only
# reaches editors that honour it; this file reaches Git itself, so the checkout
# is correct however a contributor has `core.autocrlf` set.

* text=auto

# Generated by Gradle and executed by the CI runner. Must stay LF.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts. Must stay CRLF.
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries Git must not touch. gradle-wrapper.jar is committed on purpose: it is
# what lets `./gradlew` bootstrap on a machine with no Gradle installed.
*.jar binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
